cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the paper and this archive."
type: software
title: "Code and data for: Partners, rivals, and friendly rivals in the evolution of direct reciprocity"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/martin-mn/PRFR"
authors:
  - family-names: Nowak
    given-names: Martin A.
    affiliation: Harvard University
abstract: >-
  Code and data to reproduce every figure and table of the paper and its
  Supplementary Information. The repository has five parts: the exact census,
  in the limit of rare errors, of all 65536 binary memory-two strategies at
  every symmetric two-player game, in double precision and in exact rational
  arithmetic; the family descriptions of the friendly rivals; the Wright-Fisher
  simulator as it ran on the cluster, with the seed of every replicate; the
  reduced output of the census and of the simulations; and, in notes/, the
  notes on individual strategies and cycles to which the Supplementary
  Information refers, with scripts that recompute their numbers. Each display
  item has a folder with the script that redraws or recomputes it from the
  deposited data.
keywords:
  - evolution of cooperation
  - direct reciprocity
  - repeated games
  - Nash equilibrium
  - partners
  - rivals
  - friendly rivals
  - memory-two strategies
